  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual compares only the probability of winning and the amount won, without evaluating whether one lottery has a greater concentration of probability on the favorable outcome (i.e., a more left-skewed distribution). The decision reason requires assessing the distribution's skewness — specifically, whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to the favorable outcome. In this case, Lottery A has a slightly higher probability (34% vs. 33%) of the favorable outcome, making it more left-skewed. However, the individual does not mention this or any such reasoning. Instead, the individual justifies the choice (implied or not stated) based on the higher payout in B, not on skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The justification is entirely different from the rule of the decision reason. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
