  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. While Lottery A is indeed more left-skewed (90% on 3000 € vs. 45% on 6000 €), the individual does not reference the shape of the distribution or the concept of skewness. Instead, the individual focuses on the high probability of receiving money and the perceived risk of getting nothing. The justification is based on risk aversion and probability of gain, not on skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not apply the rule that prefers the more left-skewed lottery. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
