  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not discuss the distribution of outcomes in terms of favorable vs. unfavorable probabilities or the asymmetry of the probability mass. Instead, the individual focuses on the maximum loss and the probability of losing nothing. The decision reason requires comparing the skewness (i.e., whether more probability is on favorable outcomes), which is not present in the verbal report. The individual's justification is based on risk of large losses, not on the left-skewness of the lotteries. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not apply the rule that prefers the more left-skewed lottery (which would prefer A).",
